.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DEVI_ALLOC 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_devi_alloc ,
.Nm ndi_devi_alloc_sleep ,
.Nm ndi_devi_free ,
.Nm ndi_devi_set_nodename
.Nd allocate, name, and free device nodes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_alloc
.Fa "dev_info_t *parent"
.Fa "const char *node_name"
.Fa "pnode_t nodeid"
.Fa "dev_info_t **ret_dip"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_devi_alloc_sleep
.Fa "dev_info_t *parent"
.Fa "const char *node_name"
.Fa "pnode_t nodeid"
.Fa "dev_info_t **ret_dip"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_free
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_set_nodename
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va parent
Parent nexus device node.
.It Va node_name , name
Null-terminated node name to copy.
.It Va nodeid
Firmware node identifier or one of the special identifiers below.
.It Va ret_dip
Address at which to return the newly allocated node.
.It Va dip
Node to free or rename.
.It Va flags
Reserved; pass zero.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_devi_alloc()\fP allocates a device node in the prototype state, records its
parent, copies \fBnode_name\fP, and stores the result in \fB*ret_dip\fP.
The node is not yet linked into the parent's child list, bound to a driver,
initialized by the parent, or attached.
Populate its hardware properties before binding or bringing it online.
\fBndi_devi_alloc_sleep()\fP performs the same operation with sleeping allocations.
.Pp
The special node identifiers select the following attributes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv DEVI_PSEUDO_NODEID
A nonpersistent software node, such as a node described by \fBdriver.conf\fP.
.It Dv DEVI_SID_NODEID
A persistent software-enumerated node.
.It Dv DEVI_SID_HIDDEN_NODEID
A persistent, hidden software-enumerated node.
.It Dv DEVI_SID_HP_NODEID
A persistent node marked as created by hotplug.
.It Dv DEVI_SID_HP_HIDDEN_NODEID
A persistent hotplug node that is initially hidden.
.El
.Pp
Other identifiers designate persistent PROM nodes and must be valid firmware
node identifiers.
Persistence describes the lifetime policy of the device node; it does not mean
that the node is stored across reboots.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_set_nodename()\fP copies \fBname\fP and changes the node and binding names.
Changing a name is allowed only before driver binding.
Setting the existing name succeeds without changing the node.
The \fBflags\fP argument is currently unused; pass zero.
Serialize changes to a linked node with its parent's device-tree critical
section.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_free()\fP frees a node that has not reached the initialized state.
It can undo allocation or binding, but cannot free an initialized or attached
node.
Use it for construction cleanup with no dependent children or outstanding
references; it does not report a failure from the underlying removal routine.
Use \fBndi_devi_offline()\fP with \fBNDI_DEVI_REMOVE\fP for configured nodes.
After successful freeing, the pointer must not be used.
.Sh CONTEXT
\fBndi_devi_alloc()\fP may be called from user, kernel, or low-level interrupt
context and uses non-sleeping allocations.
The other functions may be called from user or kernel context and may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_devi_alloc()\fP returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP, or \fBNDI_NOMEM\fP with
\fB*ret_dip\fP set to \fBNULL\fP.
\fBndi_devi_alloc_sleep()\fP has no return value and returns an allocated node.
\fBndi_devi_free()\fP returns \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP if the node is initialized or attached,
and \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP otherwise.
\fBndi_devi_set_nodename()\fP returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP or \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_dev_is_prom_node 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_enter 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_online 9F ,
.Xr ndi_prop_update 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
